@startgantt first_presentable_state
' Spectracs — the FIRST PRESENTABLE STATE milestone, as a schedule.
' Companion to spectracsPy/docs/SPEC_first_presentable_state.md (the prose spec) and ROADMAP.md
' (the working backlog, where these appear as NEXT TASK / PRIO 1 / PRIO 2 / PRIO 3a).
'
' The point this surfaces: the path from "the metric still moves" to "the metric and its thresholds are
' FROZEN, validated out-of-sample, and presentable to a lab owner" is ~10-12 working days, and only two
' items on it carry a real tail. Everything is sequential because each step's output is the next step's
' input: the aperture changes the optical path, so the capillary runs must come after it; the thresholds
' are derived from the capillary corpus, so they must be frozen before the validation sees any oil.
'
' Durations are EDWIN's estimates (2026-08-06), from his own bench pace, and sum to 12 working days
' - the upper end of his 10-12 range, because a plan should not be built on the optimistic end.
' ⚠ Two items carry a tail (marked red/orange): the never-rig-verified publish path and the print fit.
' Budget 13-15 days if either fights back. Effort-days, not calendar.
' Regenerate: java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg first_presentable_state.puml

printscale daily
saturday are closed
sunday are closed

' Start = TOMORROW (this was written 2026-08-06, a Thursday).
Project starts the 7th of August 2026

' ── colours ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' green  = software / desk       blue = bench measurement
' orange = build / fabrication   red  = carries a tail risk
