' ── 0 · unblock the plugin path ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
[No-op bump, then Soret trim 440-460 -> 448-460 + re-sign] as [TRIM] lasts 1 day
[TRIM] is colored in #E8756B
note bottom
  ⚠ TAIL RISK, and the only one on the critical
  path that could cost days rather than hours:
  publish->assign->load has NEVER been run end
  to end. Do the NO-OP BUMP FIRST, inside this
  day, so a failure there is not tangled with
  the metric change that follows.
end note

' ── 1 · the sample path ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[Opaque-oil test: measure f] as [FTEST] lasts 1 day
[FTEST] starts at [TRIM]'s end
[FTEST] is colored in #6BA3D6
note bottom
  Gates the aperture: undiluted oil is opaque
  in the blue, so anything above the dark
  offset is the wall-bypass path.
  f = (S_opaque - D) / (R - D)
end note

[Slide-in sample holder: design, print, fit] as [APERTURE] lasts 1 day
[APERTURE] starts at [FTEST]'s end
[APERTURE] is colored in #E8A33D
note bottom
  ⚠ TAIL RISK: assumes the print fits on the
  first or second try. Two apertures, both at
  the jar's INNER diameter.
end note

[DN guard: record min(S), warn out of window] as [DNGUARD] lasts 1 day
[DNGUARD] starts at [FTEST]'s end
[DNGUARD] is colored in #7FB069
note bottom
  §16.23.8 (design, not implemented). Two-sided:
  record min(S) per capture, warn when it leaves
  the 16 DN floor / 20-40 DN target band, propose
  the correction. Warns, never blocks.
  ⭐ Runs in PARALLEL with the aperture print (which
  has dead time) so it costs no schedule day — but it
  must land BEFORE the measurement steps, because it
  is what tells you a fill was out of range AT CAPTURE
  rather than in analysis three days later.
  ⚠ It also reads G2's finding: the capillary's +-10 %
  volume band is exactly what pushes a fill out of the
  DN window.
end note

' ── 2 · the preparation path ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[Gates G1 + G2, settle the capillary recipe] as [GATES] lasts 2 days
[GATES] starts at [APERTURE]'s end
[GATES] starts at [DNGUARD]'s end
[GATES] is colored in #6BA3D6
note bottom
  ⛔ G1 FIRST: are the capillaries heparinised?
  Heparin is insoluble in IPA and would add
  SCATTER to the one system whose open problem
  is a scattering pedestal. A failure here is a
  re-sourcing detour, not an evening.
  G2: weigh ten filled capillaries (+-10 % ID band).
end note

[Re-run green-vs-brown and green-vs-green] as [RERUN] lasts 2 days
[RERUN] starts at [GATES]'s end
[RERUN] is colored in #6BA3D6
note bottom
  On the oils ALREADY HELD (Kiendler,
  Steirerkraft, S-Budget) — NOT the validation
  panel. This is where the thresholds come from.
  Green-vs-green is the capability gate:
  d ~ 1.34 today, ~3.5-5 projected.
end note

[GO / NO-GO: is green-vs-green d >= 3 ?] as [GONOGO] happens at [RERUN]'s end

' ── 3 · freeze, then validate out-of-sample ───────────────────────────────────────
[Derive + WRITE DOWN the thresholds] as [FREEZE] lasts 1 day
[FREEZE] starts at [RERUN]'s end
[FREEZE] is colored in #7FB069
note bottom
  ⛔ Dated, written down, and NEVER re-fitted
  after the validation sees an oil. Re-fitting
  converts a validation into a demonstration.
end note

[THRESHOLDS FROZEN] as [FROZEN] happens at [FREEZE]'s end

[P3a: 8 oils, 24 fills] as [P3AMEAS] lasts 2 days
[P3AMEAS] starts at [FREEZE]'s end
[P3AMEAS] is colored in #6BA3D6
note bottom
  2 brown / 2 non-premium green / 4 premium green.
  ⭐ OUT-OF-SAMPLE: eight oils the thresholds
  have never seen. Fresh per fill (the ageing
  rule) — ~3-4 fills per evening.
end note

[Blind judging: 2 judges] as [JUDGE] lasts 1 day
[JUDGE] starts at [P3AMEAS]'s end
[JUDGE] is colored in #C58BC5
note bottom
  ⚠ Scores SEALED before any instrument output
  is revealed. Judge perceived ROAST / greenness
  — NOT "premium", which is a market label and
  may not track roast at all. Record the premium
  label separately as a second variable.
end note

[Analysis + write-up] as [WRITEUP] lasts 1 day
[WRITEUP] starts at [JUDGE]'s end
[WRITEUP] is colored in #7FB069

[FIRST PRESENTABLE STATE] as [PRESENT] happens at [WRITEUP]'s end

' ── the parked research track ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[PARKED: calibration extension + 660-680 quiet-window test] as [PARKED] lasts 3 days
[PARKED] starts at [TRIM]'s end
[PARKED] is colored in #CFCFCF
note bottom
  ⚠ PARALLEL RESEARCH TRACK — deliberately OUT
